<article class="env-lemma" id="0E8D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E8D">Lemma <span data-tag="0E8D">109.24.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $K$. Let $C$ be a smooth projective curve over $K$ with $K = H^0(C, \mathcal{O}_ C)$ having genus $g \geq 2$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$C$ has semistable reduction (Semistable Reduction, Definition <a href="/tag/0CDH" data-tag="0CDH">55.14.6</a>), or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there is a stable family of curves over $R$ with generic fibre $C$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since a stable family of curves is also prestable, it is immediate that (2) implies (1). Conversely, given a prestable family of curves over $R$ with generic fibre $C$, we can contract it to a stable family of curves by Lemma <a href="/tag/0E8A" data-tag="0E8A">109.23.4</a>. Since the generic fibre already is stable, it does not get changed by this procedure and the proof is complete. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>